WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.450 line:0
An incoming impactor concentrates energy at Earth's surface.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.860 line:0
Shock, fragmentation, and excavation displace the target rock.

00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:15.460 line:0
Excavated material, called ejecta, settles outside the crater.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.400 line:0
The depression and raised rim record the impact; later

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:25.320 line:0
erosion can modify or remove them.

00:00:26.320 --> 00:00:30.360 line:0
These relationships show relative order. Numerical ages require additional

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:32.160 line:0
evidence, such as isotopic dates.
